ter the  news broke earlier this year about the  alleged toxic workplace culture at the  blizzard side of the company many  high-profile members of the blizzard  team stepped down including president j  allen brack at the time the abk workers  alliance didn't call for resignations  like that so their call for codex  resignation is pretty significant the  abk workers alliance organized a walkout  on tuesday as well which saw over a  hundred employees leave their work from  home setups to stand outside the office  and call for codex resignation the  walkout and the general response from  employees received a lot of positive  coverage from the press and the hashtag  firebobbycodec even trended on twitter  on tuesday and bloomberg's jason  schreier reports that the ceo of sony's  playstation division jim ryan wrote an  email to employees criticizing kodak  after the news broke amidst everything  about kodak the original wall street  journal report also noted that jen  o'neil one of the co-heads appointed to  lead blizzard after brac stepped down  told activision blizzard that she didn't  believe the company could fix their  culture problem o'neill who stepped down  earlier this month less than two months  after taking the position as coley to  blizzard allegedly sent an email to  activision's legal team in which she  said that she had been sexually harassed  while working at the company and that  she was being paid less than her male  colleague despite being appointed at the  same time on wednesday ign's cat bailey  reported that o'neill was only offered a  contract with equal pay after tendering  her resignation to be clear what  allegedly happened here is that after  bombshell reports that activision  blizzard was enabling the mistreatment  and harassment of women and that women  employees were underpaid at the company  they promoted a woman to a position of  leadership and then  underpaid her  genius move amidst all this news  activision blizzard stalk took a massive